  "captions": [
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-01",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 2.0176,
      "text": "Listen to these three sentences."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-02",
      "start": 2.2134,
      "end": 3.2467,
      "text": "I am excited."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-03",
      "start": 3.4187,
      "end": 4.73,
      "text": "She is excited."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-04",
      "start": 4.9129,
      "end": 6.4831,
      "text": "They are excited."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-05",
      "start": 6.8662,
      "end": 9.5446,
      "text": "All three sentences describe the same feeling."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-06",
      "start": 9.7974,
      "end": 12.8968,
      "text": "So why do we use am, is, and are?"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-07",
      "start": 13.3169,
      "end": 15.9616,
      "text": "First, let's understand what these words mean."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-08",
      "start": 16.3795,
      "end": 18.8786,
      "text": "Am, is, and are are three forms"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-09",
      "start": 18.8786,
      "end": 21.0365,
      "text": "of the same verb: be."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-10",
      "start": 21.4518,
      "end": 24.0444,
      "text": "We use this verb to describe someone or something."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-11",
      "start": 24.2127,
      "end": 26.0277,
      "text": "For example, how someone feels,"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-12",
      "start": 26.0277,
      "end": 27.1641,
      "text": "who they are,"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-13",
      "start": 27.1641,
      "end": 28.4637,
      "text": "or where they are."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-14",
      "start": 28.8266,
      "end": 31.3561,
      "text": "In this lesson, we're using the present tense."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-15",
      "start": 31.5067,
      "end": 34.1992,
      "text": "That means we're talking about something that's true now,"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-16",
      "start": 34.1992,
      "end": 36.0657,
      "text": "or something that's generally true."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-17",
      "start": 36.3625,
      "end": 37.5919,
      "text": "For example:"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-18",
      "start": 37.5919,
      "end": 38.4342,
      "text": "\"She is happy.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-19",
      "start": 38.696,
      "end": 39.9323,
      "text": "That's how she feels now."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-20",
      "start": 40.358,
      "end": 41.6637,
      "text": "\"She is a teacher.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-21",
      "start": 41.9457,
      "end": 43.9427,
      "text": "That's something generally true about her."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-22",
      "start": 44.35,
      "end": 46.1122,
      "text": "Now, here's the important part."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-23",
      "start": 46.3481,
      "end": 48.896,
      "text": "The word we use depends on the subject."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-24",
      "start": 49.2348,
      "end": 50.2259,
      "text": "What's a subject?"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-25",
      "start": 50.3961,
      "end": 52.6929,
      "text": "It's the person or thing we're talking about."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-26",
      "start": 53.0412,
      "end": 55.7912,
      "text": "When the subject is I, we use am."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-27",
      "start": 56.0541,
      "end": 57.1878,
      "text": "\"I am happy.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-28",
      "start": 57.5637,
      "end": 61.5515,
      "text": "When the subject is he, she, or it, we use is."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-29",
      "start": 61.6587,
      "end": 62.8765,
      "text": "\"She is happy.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-30",
      "start": 63.2256,
      "end": 67.2949,
      "text": "And when the subject is you, we, or they, we use are."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-31",
      "start": 67.5013,
      "end": 68.6773,
      "text": "\"They are happy.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-32",
      "start": 69.075,
      "end": 72.6419,
      "text": "So remember, the subject tells us which form to use."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-33",
      "start": 72.9126,
      "end": 76.0613,
      "text": "In everyday English, we often make these expressions shorter."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-34",
      "start": 76.2685,
      "end": 78.0649,
      "text": "These are called contractions."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-35",
      "start": 78.2905,
      "end": 80.4197,
      "text": "\"I am\" becomes \"I'm.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-36",
      "start": 80.6146,
      "end": 83.0223,
      "text": "\"She is\" becomes \"She's.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-37",
      "start": 83.1576,
      "end": 85.5936,
      "text": "And \"They are\" becomes \"They're.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-38",
      "start": 85.8693,
      "end": 87.3736,
      "text": "The meaning stays the same."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-39",
      "start": 87.5528,
      "end": 89.4541,
      "text": "We're simply using shorter forms."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-40",
      "start": 89.8054,
      "end": 91.0937,
      "text": "Now, let's try one."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-41",
      "start": 91.4849,
      "end": 93.6737,
      "text": "\"My classmates ___ outside.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-42",
      "start": 93.9712,
      "end": 96.6417,
      "text": "Should we use am, is, or are?"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-43",
      "start": 100.1023,
      "end": 101.649,
      "text": "The answer is are!"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-44",
      "start": 101.748,
      "end": 103.726,
      "text": "\"My classmates are outside.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-45",
      "start": 103.9653,
      "end": 104.5571,
      "text": "Why?"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-46",
      "start": 104.7254,
      "end": 107.8293,
      "text": "Because \"my classmates\" refers to more than one person."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-47",
      "start": 107.9595,
      "end": 109.6195,
      "text": "We can replace it with they."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-48",
      "start": 109.7928,
      "end": 112.495,
      "text": "And we already know that \"they\" goes with \"are\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-49",
      "start": 112.8605,
      "end": 113.6685,
      "text": "Let's review."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-50",
      "start": 113.9785,
      "end": 115.2288,
      "text": "I — am."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-51",
      "start": 115.4912,
      "end": 117.9494,
      "text": "He, she, it — is."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-52",
      "start": 118.1044,
      "end": 120.6649,
      "text": "You, we, they — are."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-53",
      "start": 120.8792,
      "end": 124.1439,
      "text": "And that's how we choose between am, is, and are."
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-cap-54",
      "start": 124.3712,
      "end": 125.87,
      "text": "See you in Part 2!"
    }
  ],
